<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>OWASP on Mahmoud Adel — Application Security &amp; Offensive Security Engineer | B.Sc. Software Engineering</title><link>https://mahmoudouf.com/tags/owasp/</link><description>Recent content in OWASP on Mahmoud Adel — Application Security &amp; Offensive Security Engineer | B.Sc. Software Engineering</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 05 Dec 2024 10:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://mahmoudouf.com/tags/owasp/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>API Security Testing: Finding Vulnerabilities in Modern Web APIs</title><link>https://mahmoudouf.com/blogs/api-security-testing-vulnerabilities/</link><pubDate>Thu, 05 Dec 2024 10:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://mahmoudouf.com/blogs/api-security-testing-vulnerabilities/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;APIs are the backbone of modern applications—and a favorite target for attackers. Unlike traditional web apps, APIs often expose more functionality and data, making them high-value targets.&lt;/p&gt;
